# BS1 under Smart App Control On (release.md section 8, by-hand.md's Bootstrap, plan row 47): the
# one-liner in ConstrainedLanguage and the plain install against the served TEST build, from the
# "SAC On" snapshot (sac.suite), every user step through user-signed (Windows' own conhost.exe
# --headless: SAC blocks our unsigned hidden.exe). Both must give the SAC line (cl: it or the
# language line) and install nothing. install-high pins SAC before the elevated refusal. Restore
# uses a preinstalled saved-copy fixture from rekordbox 7.2.19, without starting rekordbox or RB
# Stems Plus. For the complete round, make "SAC On + rekordbox 7.2.19" using sac.suite --keep
# from "rekordbox 7.2.19 installed", then snapshot it. The clean "SAC On" snapshot skips Restore.
# The steps use sac/lib.ps1 so that the user steps work in ConstrainedLanguage.
#   tests/win/vm-run.sh stage
#   tests/win/vm-run.sh run "SAC On + rekordbox 7.2.19" bootstrap-sac
# Not a release.list row.
include sac/lib.ps1
need http
need file repo/scripts/bootstrap.ps1
# MODE       SECS NAME          SCRIPT
sys          120  sac-check     sac/check.ps1
user-signed  180  cl-refusal    sac/oneliner.ps1
user-signed  600  install       sac/oneliner.ps1
user-signed-high 180 install-high    sac/oneliner.ps1
sys              120 restore-fixture sac/restore-fixture.ps1
user-signed-high 300 restore         sac/restore.ps1
